-- akn:hc_1/p4 The page's caption under the table, "טבלאות שכר מהסכם 30092016 שהמשיכו בהסכם 19032017 ערכים": the tables are the September 2016 agreement's, continued by its amendment of 19.3.2017 (the header comment); no rule of its own.

§§ `בדיקת הטבלה`

-- (1) The day and the rows: §5(א)'s determining date, seniority 1 to 36.
#ASSERT `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 is updated from` EQUALS `the September 2016 determining date`
#ASSERT `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`'s `published table from` EQUALS `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 is updated from`
#ASSERT `the published labels of` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016` EQUALS range 1 36

-- (2) The tables in force on 31.8.2016 are those of 1.1.2015. To grade 6
-- every cell is theirs at the same seniority and grade; from grade 7 every
-- cell is below theirs — the grades §5(ב)(1)(א) names, where the new table
-- pays less.
GIVEN l IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the cell of 1.1.2015 to grade 6 for annex א'2` l g IS
    IF g AT MOST 6 THEN `the published cell at` `annex א'2 of 1.1.2015` l g ELSE NOTHING

`annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 beside 1.1.2015 to grade 6` MEANS
    `the published cells beside` `the cell of 1.1.2015 to grade 6 for annex א'2` `in` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`

#ASSERT null (`the published misses in` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 beside 1.1.2015 to grade 6`)
#ASSERT count `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 beside 1.1.2015 to grade 6` EQUALS 179

`the cells of annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 below 1.1.2015` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `agorot over the rule` LESS THAN 0)
           (`the published cells beside` (`the same published cell of` `annex א'2 of 1.1.2015`) `in` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`)

#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD c's `checked grade` AT LEAST 7) `the cells of annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 below 1.1.2015`
#ASSERT count `the cells of annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 below 1.1.2015` EQUALS `the published cell count of` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016` MINUS count `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 beside 1.1.2015 to grade 6`
#ASSERT `the published cells no rule reaches` (`the same published cell of` `annex א'2 of 1.1.2015`) `in` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016` EQUALS 0

-- §5(ב) at work: a teacher of grade 7 at seniority 20 on 31.8.2016, not
-- promoted, is an existing teacher — the new cell is below the old — and
-- Z is what the two tables part by, less the seniority rise each gives
-- (none here: allowances and rises left out); one of grade 6 is not.
GIVEN g IS A NUMBER, l IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `teacher at the September 2016 tables`
DECIDE `a teacher of annex א'2 at grade and seniority` g l IS
    `teacher at the September 2016 tables` WITH
        `grade before the determining date`    IS g
        `paid by the tables in force to 31.8.2016` IS TRUE
        `promoted on 1.9.2016`                 IS FALSE
        `away on 1.9.2016`                     IS `at work`
        `old table salary`                     IS fromMaybe 0 (`the published cell at` `annex א'2 of 1.1.2015` l g)
        `old allowances`                       IS 0
        `new table salary`                     IS fromMaybe 0 (`the published cell at` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016` l g)
        `new allowances`                       IS 0
        `seniority rise of the old table salary on 1.9.2016` IS 0
        `seniority rise of the new table salary on 1.9.2016` IS 0

#ASSERT `an existing teacher under §5(ב)` (`a teacher of annex א'2 at grade and seniority` 7 20)
#ASSERT `Z under §5(ב)(2)` (`a teacher of annex א'2 at grade and seniority` 7 20) EQUALS 112.17
#ASSERT NOT `an existing teacher under §5(ב)` (`a teacher of annex א'2 at grade and seniority` 6 20)

-- (3) The steps the table prints: 2% a year to the seventh year and 1%
-- from the eighth beside the rows, 7.5% to every grade in the header. Each
-- printed cell beside the cell its step makes of its neighbour, to the
-- agora (convention rounding.half).
#ASSERT map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `published rate`) (`annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`'s `published grade rates`) EQUALS LIST (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%)

`the step checks of annex א'2 of 1.9.2016` MEANS
    append (`the published cells beside` (`the published row rate of` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`) `in` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`)
           (`the published cells beside` (`the published grade rate of` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`) `in` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`)

#ASSERT count `the step checks of annex א'2 of 1.9.2016` EQUALS 403
#ASSERT count (`the published misses in` `the step checks of annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`) EQUALS 108
#ASSERT `the published worst miss in` `the step checks of annex א'2 of 1.9.2016` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the published table rises along its grades and down its rows` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`

-- (4) Not the tables of 22.2.2016. That agreement's annex א'2 is "from
-- 1.9.2016" too, with a header that rises 7.8% to grade 7; the two print
-- the same cells to grade 6 and part from grade 7.
GIVEN l IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the cell of the 22.2.2016 annex א'2` l g IS
    `the pay at grade` g (`the row labelled` `2016 annex א'2` l)

`annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 beside the 22.2.2016 annex` MEANS
    `the published cells beside` `the cell of the 22.2.2016 annex א'2` `in` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016`

#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD c's `checked grade` AT LEAST 7) (`the published misses in` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 beside the 22.2.2016 annex`)
#ASSERT count (`the published misses in` `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016 beside the 22.2.2016 annex`) EQUALS 45

-- The table at work: §46's placement on a row, and the table pay on a day.
#ASSERT `the published table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016` 36 9 EQUALS JUST 16339.11
#ASSERT `the published table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016) `annex א'2 of 1.9.2016` 36 9 EQUALS NOTHING
